coverage=[{'id':'L23-COVERAGE-01','status':'open','sourcePages':[699],'finding':'Payload, thermal effects and an external-torque convention are tested, but the explicitly listed mechanical wear, friction/backlash/stiffness drift and outdated calibration are not meaningfully assessed. Add a scenario distinguishing configuration-dependent inertia with fixed parameters from time-dependent model/calibration drift, with realistic consequences and no universal failure claim.'},{'id':'L23-COVERAGE-02','status':'open','sourcePages':[722,723],'finding':'The packet tests the matrix product with F_prime already supplied, componentwise critical gains, and the symbolic vector error equation separately. Add one complete two-joint assembly from consistent desired position/velocity/acceleration, actual state, diagonal normalized gains, coupled inertia and beta through F_prime to physical torque. Use nonzero reference acceleration and off-diagonal entries so the angle is not another recall or isolated multiplication.'},{'id':'L23-COVERAGE-03','status':'bounded_accounting_note','sourcePages':list(range(695,727)),'finding':'All 32 actual pages were inspected. Every substantive page 697–723 has citations, while 695–696 are title/outline, 724 repeats the summary, 725 lists references and 726 closes. The 62 concept records are one-per-question examination angles, not 62 independent atomic source concepts or an automatic completeness proof. Repetitions across scalar, pendulum and vector models were accepted where they test distinct sign, unit or coupling reasoning; the still-frame evidence meta-question is separately flagged.'}]
